# Conventional Commits

All commit messages MUST follow Conventional Commits.

## Format

```text
type(optional-scope): subject

optional body

optional footer
```

## Types (English)

Use one of: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`.

## Scope

- English, kebab or short noun (examples: `protocol`, `instrumentation`, `analyzer`, `sample`, `smoke`, `build`, `deps`).
- Recommended when the change targets a clear area; not mandatory for tiny chores.
- New scopes are allowed; the example list is not a closed whitelist.

## Subject

- Japanese is allowed (and preferred when it communicates intent better).
- Type and scope stay in English.
- Imperative / concise; no trailing period required.
- Focus on why when helpful; avoid dumping file lists.

## Breaking changes

Use `type(scope)!: subject` and/or a footer:

```text
BREAKING CHANGE: description
```

## Examples

```text
feat(protocol): 長さプレフィックス付きフレーミングを追加
fix(instrumentation): GRAFT_ENABLE 未設定時にパイプを立てない
chore(deps): StyleCop.Analyzers を導入
docs: M0 タスク分解を更新
```

## Agent behavior

When creating commits in this repository, draft messages in this format. Do not use free-form subjects without a type prefix.
